  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\nMixed futures with rotation in play - Russell small caps leading at +1.04% while Nasdaq slightly red. VIX down to 25.2 suggesting some risk appetite returning, but elevated volatility remains the baseline.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Iran Peace Deal Headlines</strong> - Reports of potential US-Iran memorandum signing Sunday driving oil down and risk-on flows</li>\n<li><strong>Russell 2000 Breakout</strong> - Small caps up 1.04% pre-market, testing key resistance levels</li>\n<li><strong>Energy Sector Momentum</strong> - XLE up 1.58% despite oil decline on geopolitical relief</li>\n<li><strong>Tech Divergence</strong> - XLK holding modest gains while QQQ slightly negative, watch AAPL and MSFT for direction</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-green\"><div class=\"callout-label\">✦ Bull Case</div>Iran peace talks removing geopolitical premium from markets. Small cap leadership suggests domestic focus and broadening rally beyond mega-caps.</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>Geneva peace memorandum rumors creating massive currency and commodity flows. Oil down, dollar mixed, emerging markets rallying hard.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\nClassic risk-on rotation with Energy (+1.58%), Financials (+1.27%), and Materials (+1.41%) leading despite falling oil prices. Defensive areas like Consumer Discretionary (-0.99%) and Communication Services (-0.58%) getting sold. This is peace dividend rotation, not growth rotation.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Levels That Matter</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SPY 740</strong> - Overhead resistance, break confirms continuation of relief rally</li>\n<li><strong>IWM 295</strong> - Small cap breakout level, critical for broadening thesis</li>\n<li><strong>XLE 95</strong> - Energy sector running into major resistance despite fundamental tailwinds</li>\n<li><strong>VIX 23</strong> - Below here and we're back in normal volatility regime</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>Peace talks have failed before. If Iran headlines disappoint over weekend, gap down Monday likely with energy complex and defensives leading.</div>\n\n<hr>\n<p><em>Not a prediction. A preparation. Make your plan before the bell.</em></p>",
